From f71b2431efe9f1a94c43d8deb4589114233520b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:05:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wlan0: WPA2-PSK (4-way handshake, AES/TKIP group key)

- dsiwpa.c: SHA-1, HMAC-SHA1, PBKDF2 (PMK), the PTK PRF, the EAPOL MIC,
  AES-128 and RFC 3394 key unwrap. Written for gcc 4.0.4: noinline
  helpers, memcpy instead of struct copies, word-wise XOR (byte-wise
  code crashed the compiler under -mswp-byte-writes). DSIWPA_HOST builds
  it on a PC for the test vectors in testbed/wpa_test.sh.
- dsiwifi.c: "psk PASS" (8-63 characters, never logged, wiped at
  wlan0 down); connect uses auth mode WPA2-PSK, pairwise AES, the
  group cipher from the beacon's RSN element. EAPOL messages 1 and 3
  are answered (2 and 4), the MIC is checked, the GTK is unwrapped
  with the KEK, both keys are installed with ADD_CIPHER_KEY. Group
  rekeys are answered. No data goes out before the keys are in.
- wifi-dsi-test asks for the network name and password, and runs
  /usr/bin/wpatest (the crypto as built for the DSi) first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
